---
description: Shopify embedded-app conventions
alwaysApply: true
---

# Platform

- Use Shopify authentication; do not build custom merchant authentication.
- Prefer the GraphQL Admin API for new Shopify API work.
- Use App Bridge and Polaris for embedded merchant administration.
- Use Theme App Extensions for storefront UI.
- Keep extension code lightweight and free of server business logic.

# Data Ownership

Shopify is the source of truth for products, variants, customers, orders, and
fulfillment.

The application owns shops, reviews, moderation state, widget settings,
review-request schedules, and import status.

Store only Shopify identifiers or small snapshots required by an active
workflow.

# Requests and Webhooks

- Verify every Shopify authenticated request, webhook, and app-proxy request.
- Make webhook handlers idempotent.
- Prefer webhooks to polling.
- Request only scopes required by the active phase.
- Respect Shopify GraphQL cost limits and batch related operations where
  practical.

# Merchant and Storefront Experience

- Reuse Polaris instead of recreating common admin controls.
- Keep onboarding and errors actionable.
- Keep storefront payloads small, accessible, responsive, and theme-safe.
- Never expose reviewer private data or internal errors in storefront output.

# Billing

- MVP billing uses Shopify App Pricing with only the documented Free and Pro
  plans.
- Shopify is the subscription source of truth.
- Verify plan changes before updating cached entitlements.
- Enforce published-review and review-request allowances server-side.
- Never implement off-platform payment collection.

# App Store Quality

- Classify the listing under Product reviews.
- Treat Built for Shopify as an earned status, not a self-assigned category.
- Follow current App Store and Built for Shopify requirements.
- Use the latest supported App Bridge and Shopify-native design patterns.
- Never claim the Built for Shopify badge before Shopify awards it.
